IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P9-gate`
IMPORT `P9-art-100-101`

-- Tests for Articles 100 and 101. Expected values are written from the text of the Articles and Article 113 (the group of Articles 99
-- and 100 from 2 August 2025; the group General, which includes Article 101, from 2 August 2026), never copied from the encoding's
-- output. Each function is asked on each side of its group's date. Neither Article is changed by the Omnibus (27 July 2026), so a
-- date on each side of 27 July 2026 gives the same answer.

§ `Article 100(1)`

-- args: date asked, the body is a Union institution, body, office or agency within the scope of this Regulation
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) the European Data Protection Supervisor may impose administrative fines on the body` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) the European Data Protection Supervisor may impose administrative fines on the body` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) the European Data Protection Supervisor may impose administrative fines on the body` (Date 26 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) the European Data Protection Supervisor may impose administrative fines on the body` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) the European Data Protection Supervisor may impose administrative fines on the body` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, the Supervisor is deciding on the fine or its amount, the factor
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) due regard must be given to the factor` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE `Art 100(1)(g) the annual budget of the Union institution, body, office or agency` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) due regard must be given to the factor` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE `Art 100(1)(g) the annual budget of the Union institution, body, office or agency` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) due regard must be given to the factor` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE `Art 100(1)(a) the nature, gravity and duration of the infringement and of its consequences, taking into account the purpose of the AI system concerned, as well as, where appropriate, the number of affected persons and the level of damage suffered by them` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) due regard must be given to the factor` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE `Art 100(1)(b) the degree of responsibility of the Union institution, body, office or agency, taking into account technical and organisational measures implemented by them` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) due regard must be given to the factor` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE `Art 100(1)(c) any action taken by the Union institution, body, office or agency to mitigate the damage suffered by affected persons` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) due regard must be given to the factor` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE `Art 100(1)(d) the degree of cooperation with the European Data Protection Supervisor in order to remedy the infringement and mitigate the possible adverse effects of the infringement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) due regard must be given to the factor` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE `Art 100(1)(e) any similar previous infringements by the Union institution, body, office or agency` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) due regard must be given to the factor` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE `Art 100(1)(f) the manner in which the infringement became known to the European Data Protection Supervisor, in particular whether, and if so to what extent, the Union institution, body, office or agency notified the infringement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) due regard must be given to the factor` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE `Art 100(1)(g) the annual budget of the Union institution, body, office or agency` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(1) due regard must be given to the factor` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE `Art 100(1) another factor` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Article 100(2) and (3): the infringements and the ceilings`

-- args: date asked, the infringement, the non-compliance is established
#ASSERT `Art 100 the non-compliance of the body is subject to administrative fines` (Date 1 8 2025) `Route neither` FALSE FALSE `Art 100(2) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100 the non-compliance of the body is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `Route neither` FALSE FALSE `Art 100(2) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Split site (i): not established, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Art 100 the non-compliance of the body is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `Route neither` FALSE FALSE `Art 100(2) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100 the non-compliance of the body is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `Route neither` FALSE FALSE `Art 100(3) the non-compliance of the AI system with a requirement or obligation under this Regulation other than those laid down in Article 5` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100 the non-compliance of the body is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `Route neither` FALSE FALSE `Art 100(3) the non-compliance of the AI system with a requirement or obligation under this Regulation other than those laid down in Article 5` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100 the non-compliance of the body is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `Route neither` FALSE FALSE `Art 100 another infringement` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Ceilings: paragraph 2 EUR 1 500 000, paragraph 3 EUR 750 000.
#ASSERT `Art 100 the ceiling in euros of the administrative fine on the body` `Art 100(2) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` EQUALS JUST 1500000
#ASSERT `Art 100 the ceiling in euros of the administrative fine on the body` `Art 100(3) the non-compliance of the AI system with a requirement or obligation under this Regulation other than those laid down in Article 5` EQUALS JUST 750000
#ASSERT `Art 100 the ceiling in euros of the administrative fine on the body` `Art 100 another infringement` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Article 100(4) to (7)`

-- args: date asked, the Supervisor is about to take a decision pursuant to Article 100
#ASSERT `Art 100(4) the European Data Protection Supervisor must give the body the opportunity of being heard` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(4) the European Data Protection Supervisor must give the body the opportunity of being heard` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(4) the European Data Protection Supervisor must give the body the opportunity of being heard` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 100(4) the duty of the European Data Protection Supervisor to give the body the opportunity of being heard` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 100 the European Data Protection Supervisor` DOES `Art 100(4) give the Union institution, body, office or agency the opportunity of being heard on the matter regarding the possible infringement` AT 5
-- args: date asked, the parties concerned have been able to comment on the element or circumstance
#ASSERT `Art 100(4) the decision may be based on the element or circumstance` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(4) the decision may be based on the element or circumstance` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(4) the decision may be based on the element or circumstance` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- args: date asked, there is a complainant
#ASSERT `Art 100(4) complainants must be associated closely with the proceedings` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(4) complainants must be associated closely with the proceedings` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(4) complainants must be associated closely with the proceedings` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, proceedings are conducted under this Article
#ASSERT `Art 100(5) the rights of defence of the parties concerned must be fully respected` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(5) the rights of defence of the parties concerned must be fully respected` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(5) the rights of defence of the parties concerned must be fully respected` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, the party is a party concerned, access would infringe the legitimate interest in personal data or business secrets
#ASSERT `Art 100(5) the party concerned is entitled to have access to the file of the European Data Protection Supervisor` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(5) the party concerned is entitled to have access to the file of the European Data Protection Supervisor` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(5) the party concerned is entitled to have access to the file of the European Data Protection Supervisor` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(5) the party concerned is entitled to have access to the file of the European Data Protection Supervisor` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, a fine is imposed under this Article
#ASSERT `Art 100(6) the funds collected by the fine contribute to the general budget of the Union` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(6) the funds collected by the fine contribute to the general budget of the Union` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(6) the funds collected by the fine contribute to the general budget of the Union` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(6) the fine may affect the effective operation of the body fined` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(6) the fine may affect the effective operation of the body fined` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 100(6) the fine may affect the effective operation of the body fined` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, fines were imposed or proceedings initiated during the year
#ASSERT `Art 100(7) the European Data Protection Supervisor must notify the Commission on an annual basis` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 100(7) the European Data Protection Supervisor must notify the Commission on an annual basis` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100(7) the European Data Protection Supervisor must notify the Commission on an annual basis` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 100(7) the duty of the European Data Protection Supervisor to notify the Commission on an annual basis` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 100 the European Data Protection Supervisor` DOES `Art 100(7) notify the Commission of the administrative fines imposed and of any litigation or judicial proceedings initiated` AT 5

§ `Article 101(1)`

-- args: date asked, the Commission finds intent or negligence, (a) infringed the relevant provisions, (b) failed to comply with a request under Article 91, (c) failed to comply with a measure under Article 93, (d) failed to make access available under Article 92
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) the Commission may impose a fine on the provider of the general-purpose AI model` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) the Commission may impose a fine on the provider of the general-purpose AI model` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) the Commission may impose a fine on the provider of the general-purpose AI model` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) the Commission may impose a fine on the provider of the general-purpose AI model` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) the Commission may impose a fine on the provider of the general-purpose AI model` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No intent or negligence found, or none of (a) to (d): the "when" gate fails (split site (ii)).
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) the Commission may impose a fine on the provider of the general-purpose AI model` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) the Commission may impose a fine on the provider of the general-purpose AI model` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Each side of 27 July 2026 (the Omnibus): the group General applies from 2 August 2026, so both answer NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) the Commission may impose a fine on the provider of the general-purpose AI model` (Date 26 7 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) the Commission may impose a fine on the provider of the general-purpose AI model` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The ceiling: EUR 15 000 000 or 3 % of the turnover, whichever is higher. 3 % of EUR 1 000 000 000 is 30 000 000; of EUR 100 000 000 is 3 000 000.
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) the ceiling in euros of the fine on the provider` (Date 1 8 2026) 1000000000 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) the ceiling in euros of the fine on the provider` (Date 2 8 2026) 1000000000 EQUALS JUST 30000000
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) the ceiling in euros of the fine on the provider` (Date 2 8 2026) 100000000 EQUALS JUST 15000000
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) the ceiling in euros of the fine on the provider` (Date 2 8 2026) 500000000 EQUALS JUST 15000000
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) the ceiling in euros of the fine on the provider` (Date 2 8 2026) 500000001 EQUALS JUST 15000000.03
-- args: date asked, the Commission is fixing the amount, the factor
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) regard must be had to the factor in fixing the amount` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE `Art 101(1) the nature, gravity and duration of the infringement` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) regard must be had to the factor in fixing the amount` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE `Art 101(1) the nature, gravity and duration of the infringement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) regard must be had to the factor in fixing the amount` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE `Art 101(1) the principles of proportionality and appropriateness` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) regard must be had to the factor in fixing the amount` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE `Art 101(1) commitments made in accordance with Article 93(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) regard must be had to the factor in fixing the amount` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE `Art 101(1) commitments made in relevant codes of practice in accordance with Article 56` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) regard must be had to the factor in fixing the amount` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE `Art 101(1) the nature, gravity and duration of the infringement` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 101(1) regard must be had to the factor in fixing the amount` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE `Art 101(1) another factor` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Article 101(2) to (6)`

-- args: date asked, the Commission is about to adopt a decision pursuant to paragraph 1
#ASSERT `Art 101(2) the Commission must communicate its preliminary findings to the provider and give it an opportunity to be heard` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 101(2) the Commission must communicate its preliminary findings to the provider and give it an opportunity to be heard` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101(2) the Commission must communicate its preliminary findings to the provider and give it an opportunity to be heard` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 101(2) the duty of the Commission to communicate its preliminary findings to the provider and give it an opportunity to be heard` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 101 the Commission` DOES `Art 101(2) communicate its preliminary findings to the provider of the general-purpose AI model and give it an opportunity to be heard` AT 5
-- args: date asked, effective, proportionate, dissuasive
#ASSERT `Art 101(3) the fine imposed is effective, proportionate and dissuasive` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 101(3) the fine imposed is effective, proportionate and dissuasive` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101(3) the fine imposed is effective, proportionate and dissuasive` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 101(3) the fine imposed is effective, proportionate and dissuasive` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 101(3) the fine imposed is effective, proportionate and dissuasive` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- args: date asked, a fine has been imposed, it is appropriate to communicate the information to the Board
#ASSERT `Art 101(4) the Commission must communicate the information on the fines imposed to the Board` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 101(4) the Commission must communicate the information on the fines imposed to the Board` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101(4) the Commission must communicate the information on the fines imposed to the Board` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 101(4) the Commission must communicate the information on the fines imposed to the Board` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 101(4) the duty of the Commission to communicate the information on the fines imposed to the Board` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 101 the Commission` DOES `Art 101(4) communicate information on the fines imposed to the Board` AT 5
-- args: date asked, the decision of the Commission fixes a fine under this Article
#ASSERT `Art 101(5) the Court of Justice has unlimited jurisdiction to review the decision` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 101(5) the Court of Justice has unlimited jurisdiction to review the decision` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101(5) the Court of Justice has unlimited jurisdiction to review the decision` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, the decision fixes a fine under this Article, the outcome
#ASSERT `Art 101(5) the Court of Justice may reach the outcome on the fine imposed` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE `Art 101(5) cancel the fine imposed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 101(5) the Court of Justice may reach the outcome on the fine imposed` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE `Art 101(5) cancel the fine imposed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101(5) the Court of Justice may reach the outcome on the fine imposed` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE `Art 101(5) reduce the fine imposed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101(5) the Court of Justice may reach the outcome on the fine imposed` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE `Art 101(5) increase the fine imposed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101(5) the Court of Justice may reach the outcome on the fine imposed` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE `Art 101(5) another outcome` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 101(5) the Court of Justice may reach the outcome on the fine imposed` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE `Art 101(5) cancel the fine imposed` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 101(6) the Commission must adopt implementing acts containing detailed arrangements and procedural safeguards for proceedings` (Date 1 8 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 101(6) the Commission must adopt implementing acts containing detailed arrangements and procedural safeguards for proceedings` (Date 2 8 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 101(6) the duty of the Commission to adopt implementing acts containing detailed arrangements and procedural safeguards for proceedings` (Date 2 8 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 101 the Commission` DOES `Art 101(6) adopt implementing acts containing detailed arrangements and procedural safeguards for proceedings` AT 5
-- args: date asked, the implementing act is adopted in accordance with the examination procedure of Article 98(2)
#ASSERT `Art 101(6) the implementing act is adopted in the way the paragraph requires` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 101(6) the implementing act is adopted in the way the paragraph requires` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 101(6) the implementing act is adopted in the way the paragraph requires` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Seam S14: Article 2(2) cuts off this Article for a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products`

-- Expected values written from Article 2(2): "For AI systems classified as high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 6(1) related to products covered by
-- the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I, only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (as enacted: Article 6(1),
-- Articles 102 to 109 and Article 112). Per function: the Annex I route with Section B products is cut off (JUST FALSE), with or without the integration fact;
-- products outside Section B leave the provision to answer for itself; an Annex III system is not spoken to by Article 2(2); before the group applies, NOTHING.
-- args after the system: the products are covered by Section B legislation, the requirements have been integrated in it.
-- Art 100 the non-compliance of the body is subject to administrative fines
#ASSERT `Art 100 the non-compliance of the body is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` TRUE FALSE `Art 100(2) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 100 the non-compliance of the body is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` TRUE TRUE `Art 100(2) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 100 the non-compliance of the body is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` FALSE FALSE `Art 100(2) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100 the non-compliance of the body is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III` TRUE TRUE `Art 100(2) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Each infringement of Article 100, asked on 2 August 2025 (the first day of the group): with the Annex I route and Section B products the fine of Article 100 is cut off (JUST FALSE); with other products it is answered as for any system (JUST TRUE).
#ASSERT `Art 100 the non-compliance of the body is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` TRUE FALSE `Art 100(2) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 100 the non-compliance of the body is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` FALSE FALSE `Art 100(2) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 100 the non-compliance of the body is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` TRUE FALSE `Art 100(3) the non-compliance of the AI system with a requirement or obligation under this Regulation other than those laid down in Article 5` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 100 the non-compliance of the body is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I` FALSE FALSE `Art 100(3) the non-compliance of the AI system with a requirement or obligation under this Regulation other than those laid down in Article 5` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

